@format 1
@id logging.emit-entry
@title Emit log entry
@area 9. Logging
@entry input
@summary Create a structured trace entry, publish it to live viewers, enqueue its text, and flush batches to the active log file.
@section II. Functionality
@flow TB
@related logging.open-feed
@tag logging
@tag trace

@alias trace = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LTrace
@alias traceWriter = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LTraceWriter

[input] Component records a trace <input>
- Receive a trace kind, summary, optional detail, and duration @ trace.LTraceRecord(...)
> filter

[filter] Check category <decision>
- Determine whether this trace kind is enabled @ trace.LTraceCheck(...)
? "Category is enabled" > publish
? "Category is disabled" > omitted

[publish] Publish trace <process>
- Create and append the structured in-memory trace entry @ trace.LTraceRecord(...)
- Notify live log subscribers @ trace.LTraceRecord(...)
- Format and enqueue the entry for disk writing @ traceWriter.LTraceWriterRecord(...)
> write

[write] Persist batch <storage>
- Start the background writer when first needed @ traceWriter.LTraceWriterStart(...)
- Append queued entries in bounded batches and record dropped-entry counts @ traceWriter.LTraceWriterRun(...)
- Flush the writer after an idle interval @ traceWriter.LTracePersistRun(...)
> result

[omitted] Entry omitted <output>
= Disabled verbose-category entries are neither published nor persisted.

[result] Entry available <output>
= The entry is visible to live subscribers and durable after the writer flushes.
